                                                EXPERIMENT 1.1-     CONTAINS DUPLICATE PROBLEM  [LEET CODE PROBLEM 217]
Aim - Given an integer array nums, return true if any value appears at least twice in the array, and return false if every element is distinct.

Algorithm -  Contains Duplicate
Start.
Take the input array nums.
Sort the array in ascending order.
Traverse the array from the second element (i = 1) to the last element.
Compare the current element nums[i] with the previous element nums[i-1].
If both elements are equal, return true (duplicate found).
If the loop finishes without finding any duplicate, return false.
End.

CODE - class Solution {
public:
    bool containsDuplicate(vector<int>& nums) {
        sort(nums.begin(), nums.end());

        for(int i=1; i < nums.size();i++) {
            if (nums[i]==nums[i-1]){
                return true;
            }
        }

        return false;
    }
};  




